---
// src/pages/terms.astro
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "September 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions — CloudGrid Africa"
  description="Terms governing use of cloudgridafrica.com. Separate from any signed engagement agreement for CloudGrid Africa's engineering services."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content" class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="cga-container">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <p class="cga-eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] text-ink-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

        <div class="prose prose-invert prose-headings:font-semibold prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-headings:text-white prose-p:text-[14.5px] prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-p:text-ink-secondary prose-a:text-signal-blue prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline prose-strong:text-ink-primary prose-li:text-ink-secondary prose-hr:border-midnight-border mt-10 max-w-none">
          <p>
            <em>
              This page governs use of the cloudgridafrica.com website only. It is provided
              as a plain-language reference and is not a substitute for legal advice. It
              does not constitute, replace, or modify any signed statement of work, master
              services agreement, or engagement contract between CloudGrid Africa and a
              client — those documents govern the actual delivery of cloud engineering,
              cybersecurity, or compliance services and take precedence over anything on
              this page.
            </em>
          </p>

          <h2>Acceptance of these terms</h2>
          <p>
            By accessing cloudgridafrica.com, you agree to these terms. If you do not
            agree, please do not use the site.
          </p>

          <h2>What this site is for</h2>
          <p>
            This website describes CloudGrid Africa's cloud engineering, cybersecurity, and
            compliance services, publishes editorial content on our blog, and provides a
            way to request a consultation. Nothing published here — including the
            AI-assisted chat widget — constitutes a binding quote, contractual commitment,
            or professional assessment of your own systems. Specific engagements are
            scoped and agreed separately, in writing, following a consultation.
          </p>

          <h2>The chat widget specifically</h2>
          <p>
            The chat widget on this site is an AI assistant grounded in publicly available
            information about CloudGrid Africa. It cannot see, assess, or make claims about
            your own infrastructure or security posture, does not provide pricing, and
            should not be relied upon as professional advice. If you describe what sounds
            like an active security incident in the chat, we ask you to call
            +254 721 656 835 directly rather than continue the conversation there.
          </p>

          <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            The site's design, written content, and code are the property of CloudGrid
            Africa unless otherwise credited. You may not reproduce, redistribute, or use
            our branding, case study content, or blog articles for commercial purposes
            without written permission.
          </p>

          <h2>Case studies and figures</h2>
          <p>
            Case study outcomes, metrics, and client names referenced on this site (for
            example, under "Case Studies") reflect specific past engagements and are not
            guarantees of results for any future client. Results vary by project scope,
            existing infrastructure, and organisational context.
          </p>

          <h2>No warranty on website availability</h2>
          <p>
            We aim to keep this website available and accurate, but do not guarantee
            uninterrupted access, and are not liable for losses arising from temporary
            unavailability, typographical errors, or reliance on informational content
            published here (including blog posts and the daily auto-generated brief, which
            is explicitly labelled as such).
          </p>

          <h2>Third-party links</h2>
          <p>
            This site links to third-party services (for example, Resend, Anthropic, and
            Open-Meteo, described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>) and to news
            sources in the Tech Intelligence Hub. We are not responsible for the content or
            practices of external sites.
          </p>

          <h2>Governing law</h2>
          <p>
            These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Kenya. Any dispute
            arising from use of this website falls under the jurisdiction of the Kenyan
            courts.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these terms as the site changes. Continued use of the site after
            an update constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
          </p>

          <hr />
          <p>
            Questions about these terms? <a href="/#contact">Contact us</a> or read our
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
